From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt76x02: remove the stations after the tx flush in a restart

mt76x02_watchdog_reset() removes the stations, unpublishing their WCIDs,
before it flushes the hardware tx queues and the tx status entries. The
frames still queued are then completed with no station, and
ieee80211_tx_status_ext() returns their airtime (AQL) to the global
counters only, leaving it pending on the station. The station survives the
restart, so that airtime is never returned; once it reaches the AQL high
limit, mac80211 stops handing the station's frames on that AC to the
driver, while the station stays associated.

After a restart caused by a stuck tx queue, the stuck frames are completed
this way. On an MT7612E AP with a phone uploading, the phone's pending BE
airtime was 4736 us after one restart and 12004 us (the high limit is
12000 us) after two more, with the global pending at 0 and the hardware
queues empty; its BE queue was no longer dequeued until it reassociated.

Remove the stations only after the flush. The key PN sync and the
interface masks stay before the hardware reset. On mt76x2e, frames
completed during the flush are untracked ones, reported without tx info,
or tracked ones, reported as acked (MT_DRV_IGNORE_TXS_FAILED), so they do
not feed the low-ack detection.

In a subsequent MT7612E AP comparison, pending BE airtime drained to
0-4 us after five resets with station removal after the flush. With
station removal before the flush, it remained at 12004 us after three
resets, with the global pending counter and hardware queues empty and
the station BE queue no longer dequeued. This was one sequential phase
per ordering, not independent trials for each reset.

Fixes: 0fe88644c060 ("mt76: improve tx status codepath")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/mt76x02_mmio.c
+++ b/mt76x02_mmio.c
@@ -415,8 +415,6 @@
 
 static void mt76x02_reset_state(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
 {
-	int i;
-
 	lockdep_assert_held(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 
 	clear_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &dev->mphy.state);
@@ -425,6 +423,21 @@
 	ieee80211_iter_keys_rcu(dev->mt76.hw, NULL, mt76x02_key_sync, NULL);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
+	dev->mt76.vif_mask = 0;
+	dev->mt76.beacon_mask = 0;
+}
+
+/* Only after the frames left in the hardware queues have been completed:
+ * mac80211 returns their airtime (AQL) to the station given in the tx
+ * status. Without one it stays pending on the station for good, and after
+ * a few restarts under load the station's tx queues are no longer served.
+ */
+static void mt76x02_reset_stations(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < MT76x02_N_WCIDS; i++) {
 		struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
 		struct ieee80211_vif *vif;
@@ -456,9 +469,6 @@
 		if (ps)
 			set_bit(MT_WCID_FLAG_PS, &msta->wcid.flags);
 	}
-
-	dev->mt76.vif_mask = 0;
-	dev->mt76.beacon_mask = 0;
 }
 
 static void mt76x02_watchdog_reset(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
@@ -515,6 +525,9 @@
 
 	mt76_tx_status_check(&dev->mt76, true);
 
+	if (restart)
+		mt76x02_reset_stations(dev);
+
 	mt76x02_mac_start(dev);
 
 	if (dev->ed_monitor)
